                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Biochemistry is a fundamental life science course that comprehensively elucidates the structure and function of biological macromolecules at the molecular level, as well as the metabolic pathways, interrelationships, and regulatory mechanisms of the three major nutrients. This course, combined with biochemistry laboratory classes, will help students comprehensively master the basic theories and experimental skills of biochemistry.</p>
<p>The course content is based on the structure and function of macromolecules such as proteins, nucleic acids, carbohydrates, and lipids, providing a holistic understanding of the metabolic processes and regulatory mechanisms of macromolecules within the body.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
